Coverage review — DONE

**Known fixes checked before code review:** Android’s [build-variant guidance](https://developer.android.com/build/build-variants) supports separate Play listings through distinct application IDs; the plan’s `dev` build type does this, although Google’s example uses product flavors. Android’s [FileHandler](https://developer.android.com/reference/java/util/logging/FileHandler) documents process-unique rotating files; the plan uses the same separation, but proposes its own writer. Android’s [FileProvider guidance](https://developer.android.com/training/secure-file-sharing) requires a content URI and temporary read access; the plan names FileProvider but omits the share-intent details.

### 1. Enumerated populations — FOUND-GAP

- **Take endings:** The list equates endings with audio deletion. A cancel before binding, a processing cancel, a startup failure, and an empty final text can end without those deletion sites ([coordinator:1035](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:1035), [1087](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:1087), [1137](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:1137), [983](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:983); [plan:167](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:167)). **Add:** “Enumerate terminal arbiter commits independently of audio retirement. Log the take id and terminal reason for every winning commit, including endings with no audio file.”
- **Take IDs and word stages:** ASR initializes on service creation, before a take ID exists ([AsrService:238](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/asr/AsrService.kt:238)); polish can answer before registry registration ([PolishService:180](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/polish/PolishService.kt:180), [194](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/polish/PolishService.kt:194)). Cleanup performs several rewrites inside one call ([DeterministicCleanup:121](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/cleanup/DeterministicCleanup.kt:121)). **Add:** “Mark pre-take model initialization `take=-`; carry the supplied take id through polish’s pre-registration fallback and delivery paths. Emit file-only words after each enabled cleanup family, including a recovered result.”
- **Package and task references:** The plan’s package override covers the harness constant, but its persisted switch debt explicitly has no package identity ([wispr_eyes.py:1423](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/uat/wispr_eyes.py:1423)). The remaining task references are covered under axes 3 and 6. **Add:** “Key Wispr Eyes’ persisted debts by package as well as device, and refuse to restore a debt against another package.”

### 2. Release pipeline — FOUND-GAP

- **Partial publication loses the promised fallback artifact:** The signed bundle and receipt upload runs only after `publish.py` succeeds ([play-internal.yml:78](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/.github/workflows/play-internal.yml:78), [80](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/.github/workflows/play-internal.yml:80)); the plan promises that artifact when Dev publication fails ([plan:198](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:198)). **Add:** “Persist each signed, verified bundle and its per-app publication state even when the other app fails; upload both signed bundles and the partial receipt with `if: always()`.”
- **Per-app checks and reports need explicit scope:** The current publisher checks one package, version, debuggable flag, track, draft status and signed hash ([publish.py:38](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/release/publish.py:38), [98](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/release/publish.py:98), [111](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/release/publish.py:111), [136](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/release/publish.py:136)); the receipt and upload path name only Release ([test_receipt.py:4](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/release/test_receipt.py:4), [play-internal.yml:43](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/.github/workflows/play-internal.yml:43)). **Add:** “For each named receipt row, verify its own artifact hash, manifest package, version code, non-debuggable flag, existing track maximum, upload hash, expected draft/completed status and read-back. Require fresh nonzero Release and Dev test XML and upload both report directories.”

### 3. Build — FOUND-GAP

- **Source-set wiring and cache inputs:** D2 specifies shared `java` wiring, while its provider manifest and path XML also need variant wiring ([plan:116](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:116), [131](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:131)). JVM tasks currently declare only debug, androidTest and JNI extra inputs ([build.gradle.kts:103](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/build.gradle.kts:103)). **Add:** “Wire the shared log Java, manifest and resources into Debug and Dev, and exclude all three from Release. Add `src/locallog` and `src/release` to the shape test’s declared Gradle inputs.”
- **Dev validation before merge:** PR CI runs Debug only ([check.sh:19](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/ci/check.sh:19)); listing `testDevUnitTest` proves only that the task exists ([plan:247](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:247)). **Add:** “Run `testDevUnitTest`, `bundleDev` and `lintDev` on the PR before merge, and require a nonzero Dev test receipt.” The existing workflow passes both telemetry keys to Gradle ([build.sh:15](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/release/build.sh:15)); no gap found there.

### 4. Privacy enforcement — FOUND-GAP

- **Consumer archive check:** The proposed AAB check names only the sink class, although G7 also excludes archive code ([plan:116](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:116), [0: G7](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:51)). **Add:** “Inspect the Consumer AAB for the archive implementation and provider declaration as well as the log sink; require all to be absent.”
- **Shape test can miss content-bearing interpolation:** Its own documented limit permits an unconventionally named throwable to pass ([DiagnosticsShapeTest:28](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/test/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DiagnosticsShapeTest.kt:28)); polish interpolates an outcome into logcat ([PolishService:378](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/polish/PolishService.kt:378)). Whether that outcome renders words is **NOT VERIFIED** from allowed files. **Add:** “Pin every object interpolation sent to `DebugLogger`, including polish outcomes, to a content-free rendering; test with sentinel dictated words that neither logcat nor telemetry receives them.”

