### 7. Tests — FOUND-GAP

- **Existence and shape checks can pass without behavior:** A task-list check passes without running Dev tests ([plan:247](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:247)). Counting `LocalLog.words` calls can pass if calls remain but their text is empty; a direct sink test can pass if the `DebugLogger` handoff is removed ([plan:168](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:168), [230](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:230)). A migration test can pass while new timing fields are never written. **Add:** “Use a sentinel take through `DebugLogger` and each word stage; assert its actual text and take id in the shared log. Assert a completed History row contains measured timing values, including the later insertion outcome. Run each stated removal revert against these outcome assertions.”
- **Cancelled-take oracle is impossible:** §11 requests one cancelled take, then requires every take to have raw, cleanup, polish and final words ([plan:238](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:238), [239](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/docs/feature-requests/issue-378-2026-09-27-dev-app-local-log.md:239)). **Add:** “For completed takes, require all reached word and timing stages. For a cancelled take, require its take id, last reached stage and terminal reason; require no stages after cancellation.”